{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Operator-approved scope\nImplement the finalized 2026-09-02 scope from the ticket comments: rebar LLM gate operations emit lightweight keepalive lines synchronously at existing progress seams so supervising stall watchdogs are not silent for an entire multi-call gate phase.\n\n## Implementation plan\n1. Add a small shared LLM keepalive helper with `KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL_S = 25.0` and a single last-emit-timestamp comparison. It logs at WARNING so the line reaches stderr at rebar's default effective log level (WARNING) without `REBAR_LOG_LEVEL`.\n2. Guard the timestamp comparison/update with a simple in-process lock so coalescing is race-free if runner, tool, or workflow emit sites are crossed concurrently.\n3. Emit through that helper at the primary per-LLM-call seam in `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, including operation/phase name, call index when available, and elapsed seconds only.\n4. Ensure keepalive content excludes prompt text, model responses, tool arguments, and tool payloads.\n5. Emit through the same helper inside the per-tool `call_tool` boundary in `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py`: the `_MemoNudgeToolset` and `_SteeringToolset` wrappers built by `_memo_toolsets` / `_steering_toolsets`, which fire per tool call during the agentic loop on the event-loop thread. Do not use post-run helpers such as `log_call_success` for this requirement.\n6. Emit through the same helper at workflow-step boundaries in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/interpreter.py`, adjacent to the existing per-step `_t_step` / `_dispatch(...)` timing boundary where workflow steps are actually iterated.\n7. Use the shared elapsed-time coalescing so bursts of fast tool/step calls do not produce one line per call.\n8. Keep the change purely additive: no background daemon thread, no progress-gating/stall escalation/health withdrawal, no total-runtime cap, and no change to existing timeout behavior, preserving ADR 0089.\n9. Keep `KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL_S` as a fixed module constant rather than config surface because the approved scope explicitly requested no new config unless trivial; supervisor-specific tuning remains the supervisor's no-output budget, documented below.\n10. Add a short warning to gate documentation that gate ops can exceed common 600s supervisor stall budgets while silent between calls; the new keepalive mitigates multi-call silence, but a single very long request can still exceed a budget. Note `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_S=600` is per request and close can make many requests, so supervisors may need larger no-output budgets.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Default-level keepalive: a gate/agentic-loop path crossing per-call progress emits at least one keepalive line to stderr/log capture at the default WARNING level. Verified by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_keepalive.py::test_runner_keepalive_reaches_default_warning_level -q` and by an entrypoint stderr-handler smoke check without `REBAR_LOG_LEVEL`.\n- [x] Coalescing: rapid tool-call/step bursts do not emit one line per call. Verified by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_keepalive.py::test_tool_keepalives_are_coalesced -q`.\n- [x] Concurrent coalescing: simultaneous emit attempts crossing the guarded timestamp comparison still coalesce to one keepalive for an interval. Verified by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_keepalive.py::test_concurrent_keepalives_share_one_interval -q`.\n- [x] Content safety: keepalive lines include only operation/phase name, call index where available, and elapsed seconds. Verified by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_keepalive.py -q`.\n- [x] ADR 0089 compatibility: no timer thread, total-runtime cap, timeout change, or interruption of slow-but-alive calls is introduced. Verified by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py::test_no_total_runtime_timer_mechanism tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py::test_slow_but_alive_server_completes_under_read_timeout -q`.\n- [x] Documentation: the supervisor stall-budget warning lands in the gate/config docs. Verified by review of `docs/plan-review-gate.md` and `docs/config.md` plus `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`.\n\n## Testing\nTargeted RED/GREEN commands:\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_keepalive.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py::test_no_total_runtime_timer_mechanism tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py::test_slow_but_alive_server_completes_under_read_timeout -q`\n\nReview preflight commands:\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n\nEmpirical default-level check:\n- Run a fast deterministic gate/runner invocation without `REBAR_LOG_LEVEL` and assert the keepalive is written through logging at WARNING, which reaches stderr/log capture under the default effective level.\n\n## Portability\nThe implementation is pure Python logging plus deterministic unit tests. It does not depend on any CI provider, external daemon, terminal feature, or platform-specific supervisor, satisfying project portability."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788395753194706045,"uuid":"7de287ed-e54d-4edd-a7c1-fa0432e2d70f"}